              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 22,
                "start": 22
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Stoler, petitioner argues that the separate crime and separate punishment provision of \u00a7\u202f924(c) requires a distinct sentencing analysis."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Stoler",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "5de4b8ccd0980e864938fd7353c72ac7b0445749ac24ebe82c32e39870457bb2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-5de4b8ccd098-0002-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 52,
                "start": 52
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Stoler, petitioner further contends that district courts have no affirmative ban on applying \u00a7\u202f924(c) sentencing when considering predicate offenses, emphasizing judicial discretion and parsimony."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner (Levon Dean, Jr.) Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Yang",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "5de4b8ccd0980e864938fd7353c72ac7b0445749ac24ebe82c32e39870457bb2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-5de4b8ccd098-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 25,
                "start": 25
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Yang, respondent argues that, when read together with the Sentencing Reform Act, Congress\u2019s intent in \u00a7\u202f924(c) is clear and supports the statutory scheme."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Yang",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "5de4b8ccd0980e864938fd7353c72ac7b0445749ac24ebe82c32e39870457bb2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-5de4b8ccd098-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 39,
                "start": 39
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Yang, respondent further maintains that Congress intended judges to determine the aggregate length of sentences\u2014whether they run concurrently or consecutively\u2014when multiple offenses carry imprisonment terms."
        }
      ],
